# Party banter at the Wizard of Wines. Each node opens with an `if` gate: the node is eligible only while its
# condition holds. Party members speak only through interjections; a line plays if a matching member is present.
# Ratatoille has no lines here: his reaction to the place is a quest scene of its own.

~ banter_wine_country
if flag.davian_met and not flag.winery_reclaimed and name:kip_smudgewick and name:thistle
interject name:kip_smudgewick: Not one bottle left whole, and the vines are sick. I know a blighted row when I see one. You don't forget it.
interject name:thistle: Druids. Smash his stores, sour his fields, then wait. That's how Grandda starves out a badger.
interject name:kip_smudgewick: Oh, lovely. I was hoping they'd be careless.
endif
-> END

~ banter_ravens
if flag.davian_met and not flag.keepers_allied
interject tag:scholarly: Lycanthropy, but ravens. The literature is very thin. I want everyone to know I am being extremely restrained about asking them questions.
interject tag:blunt: Good. Keep being restrained.
endif
-> END

~ banter_father_and_son
if flag.elvir_story_heard and not flag.martikovs_reconciled and name:godrick_pendlebrook and name:liriel_dawnsong
interject name:godrick_pendlebrook: Two lads went up that hill. One came home. And the old man can't forgive the one who did.
interject name:liriel_dawnsong: Grief wants a door to knock on. Adrian is the only door left in that house.
endif
-> END

~ banter_stones
if flag.winery_stone_hiding_told and not flag.winery_stone_recovered and not name:ratatoille
interject class:wizard: Three stones that make vines grow where nothing should. Payment for one winter's lodging. That wizard either loved wine more than anyone ever has, or the stones were the cheapest thing in his pockets.
interject tag:curious: Or he's coming back for the casks.
endif
-> END

~ banter_reconciled
if flag.martikovs_reconciled and name:godrick_pendlebrook and name:wren_featherfoot
interject name:godrick_pendlebrook: When the old man gave Adrian the press. His face. I'm crying, and I don't care who sees. Knights are allowed.
interject name:wren_featherfoot: It's the vinegar. Whole place reeks of it. That's all this is.
interject name:liriel_dawnsong: It isn't the vinegar, Wren.
endif
-> END

~ banter_wine_flows
if flag.winery_wine_flows
interject tag:cheerful: First real wine in this whole valley, and we're the reason. I'm going to be insufferable about this.
interject tag:blunt: You were already insufferable.
interject tag:cheerful: Now I'll have a reason.
endif
-> END

~ banter_kept_the_fee
if flag.winery_strongbox_kept
interject class:cleric: We took the old man's strongbox in a war he was losing. I'd like that remembered when we're being proud of ourselves.
interject class:rogue: Remembered. It was a very good lock, though.
endif
-> END

~ banter_keepers
if flag.keepers_allied and name:thistle and name:wren_featherfoot
interject name:thistle: That raven's been on every fence we've passed for three days. I asked it. It says we're family now.
interject name:wren_featherfoot: Adopted again. Last time it was an old elf with a stick. Birds are better. Birds don't make you sweep.
endif
-> END
